  "rationale": "Blocking three steps works: fileServer:lateralMovement, dbLogin:authenticate and vaultRead:collection. Blocking fileServer stops codeRepo, and with jumpHost also dead it stops mailArchive. Blocking dbLogin kills jumpHost, so shareMount, mailArchive and serviceAccount fail, and it also kills secretsManager. Blocking vaultRead removes the last route, which runs through printServer from memoryDump. Two blocks are not enough. These three attack chains share no steps: (1) iotDevice -> sshKey -> fileServer -> codeRepo, an all-OR chain; (2) supplychain -> memoryDump -> printServer -> vaultRead, an all-OR chain; (3) dmzWeb + tokenCache -> dbLogin -> jumpHost -> shareMount. Chains (1) and (2) depend only on their own steps, so each needs its own block. Any block that stops chain (3), including tokenCache, lies on neither of the first two, so at least 3 blocks are required."
 },
